A conversion provider whose source expression names an undefined identifier: value
positions get no recorded type at all (unlike type positions, which record Invalid), so
the directive fails loudly instead of silently vanishing. A single typo suffices to hit
this. No redeclaration needed.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type T int

//plumb:build
var _ T = Undeclared
